course: dictionary
lesson: 5402
title: Kosher: food laws and fair deals
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a special subject, like religion or food. «Kosher means allowed by Jewish food law; kosher food laws include no pork and not mixing meat and milk.» The sentence gives the clues: food laws, no pork, and meat and milk kept apart. So kosher is about what Jewish law allows people to eat.
explain: A kosher shop or kitchen sells or makes kosher food, so the word can also describe places. Check the words around it: if the sentence talks about rules for food, kosher means the food follows those rules.
explain: Kosher also has an informal meaning. «Is this deal kosher?» is not asking about food at all. The words deal and is tell you it means genuine and honest. If someone says a plan is «not quite kosher», they mean it seems suspicious.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Kosher» means allowed by Jewish food law, and prepared in the right way.
fact: A kosher kitchen keeps meat and milk apart, and pork is not eaten.
fact: In informal speech, «kosher» means genuine, honest or acceptable.
fact: «Not kosher» in informal speech means suspicious or not allowed.
exercise: «Kosher food laws include no pork.» What does kosher mean in this sentence? | *Allowed by Jewish food law | Made from fish only | Very cheap and easy to buy
exercise: Someone asks, «Is this deal kosher?» What are they asking? | Is the deal on sale today? | Is the deal the right size? | Is the deal far away? | *Is the deal genuine and honest?
exercise: Copy the word that tells you the food follows religious rules: «The shop sells kosher food.» | shop | sells | *kosher | food
test: «A kosher kitchen keeps meat and milk apart.» What does kosher suggest about this kitchen? | *It follows Jewish food law | It sells only bread | It is very clean and shiny
test: «Something seems not quite kosher about that plan.» What does not quite kosher suggest? | A plan full of fresh bread | A very clean and shiny plan | *Suspicious, something is not right
exam: Which sentence uses kosher to mean genuine or honest? | Pork is not eaten under kosher law. | *Is this deal kosher? | A kosher kitchen keeps meat and milk apart. | The shop sells kosher food.
